    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "“Fallowfield” is a delightful family home dating from the 1950’s. Occupying an elevated position and set within mature gardens, it is located just above Howth Village close to the summit of Howth. Inside, it has retained all of its original period character and charm while enjoying pleasant views over the surrounding landscape outside, towards Irelands Eye and Lambay Islands below. \r\n \r\nThe accommodation extends to approx. c.187.6 sq.m / c.2,019 sq.ft and briefly comprises an entrance hall, living room, family room, dining room, kitchen/breakfast room, utility room and guest WC at ground floor level. Upstairs there are three bedrooms, including a large principal bedroom with a shower room en-suite and there is a main family bathroom. The landing has a large dormer window revealing a spectacular view – an ideal work from home space could be created here. \r\n\r\n \r\nThe property has been well maintained although it will benefit from energy efficiency upgrading and modernising internally. The interior is bright with comfortable sized rooms throughout, while the panoramic views from the rear are quite special. \r\n\r\nFallowfield is surrounded by generous elevated gardens. Both the front and rear gardens are substantial in size, offering excellent outdoor amenity space to compliment this home.\r\n \r\nThe location is highly convenient, within easy reach of Howth Village, the harbour, DART station, local shops, cafés, restaurants, schools and a wide range of sporting and recreational amenities. The area is also well known for its coastal walks and scenic surroundings.\r\n\r\nFallowfield offers a rare opportunity to acquire a detached home on a large site in one of Howth’s most sought-after locations.\r\n\r\nViewing is available by appointment with Gallagher Quigley at info@gallagherquigley.ie or tel : +35318183000.\r\n \r\n\r\nSpecial features \r\n\r\nThere is a large detached snooker/games room to the side providing additional flexible space suitable for a variety of uses.\r\n\r\nPanoramic views of surrounding landscape towards Irelands Eye and Lambay.\r\n\r\nc. 2019 square feet of floor area\r\n\r\nWonderful location in private setting close to all amenities"
      },
